WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.502
-Well, hey, guys,
it is March, late March,

00:00:02.502 --> 00:00:06.940
and that means that it's time
for people to --

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:08.841
Tariq, you okay?

00:00:08.841 --> 00:00:10.476
Seem a little bothered.

00:00:10.476 --> 00:00:12.111
-No, I'm good.

00:00:12.111 --> 00:00:14.914
[ Scattered laughter ]

00:00:14.914 --> 00:00:17.450
-You sure? You don't seem good.

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:19.719
-No, I'm just, you know,
thinking of some new entries

00:00:19.719 --> 00:00:22.722
for my irk list.

00:00:22.722 --> 00:00:24.390
-Irk list? What's an irk list?

00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:26.258
-Come on, man. You know,
it's a list that I keep

00:00:26.258 --> 00:00:28.060
of things that annoy me.

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:29.095
Random stuff.

00:00:29.095 --> 00:00:31.030
You know what?
I'll just show you.

00:00:31.030 --> 00:00:33.399
It's time for
"Tariq's Irk List"!

00:00:33.399 --> 00:00:35.435
-♪ "Tariq's Irk List" ♪

00:00:35.435 --> 00:00:39.672
♪ Of the things that irk Tariq ♪

00:00:39.672 --> 00:00:42.074
-So, my daughter
woke me up last night

00:00:42.074 --> 00:00:43.443
because she heard a noise
in her room.

00:00:43.443 --> 00:00:46.679
I go, "What do you
want me to do?

00:00:46.679 --> 00:00:49.181
You know I haven't been
eating meat, girl. I'm weak."

00:00:49.181 --> 00:00:50.416
-[ Laughs ] What?

00:00:50.416 --> 00:00:52.685
-So, she says she thinks
she heard a ghost.

00:00:52.685 --> 00:00:55.721
Now, no disrespect to people who
believe in the supernatural --

00:00:55.721 --> 00:00:57.157
I mean, I think I do.

00:00:57.157 --> 00:01:00.493
I definitely believe energy
just transfers and never dies.

00:01:00.493 --> 00:01:04.129
But I don't really buy into
the concept of the traditional,

00:01:04.129 --> 00:01:09.201
mischievous, "boo," Scooby-Doo
variety of ghosts, Jimmy.

00:01:09.201 --> 00:01:11.470
So, I go, "Child --"

00:01:11.470 --> 00:01:13.740
I'm terrible with names.

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:15.541
I go --
-Your own child?

00:01:15.541 --> 00:01:17.343
-Yeah, I --
-Your own --

00:01:17.343 --> 00:01:18.711
-It leaves me.

00:01:18.711 --> 00:01:21.681
I go, "Child,
there's no way ghosts exist."

00:01:21.681 --> 00:01:23.316
And she's all,
"How do you know?"

00:01:23.316 --> 00:01:26.085
which at this point, is pretty
much all she ever says to me.

00:01:26.085 --> 00:01:27.887
I mean, she's 15 years old.

00:01:27.887 --> 00:01:30.623
But it irks me that she demands

00:01:30.623 --> 00:01:33.626
I produce proof to support
anything I ever said --

00:01:33.626 --> 00:01:35.961
footnotes, bibliography,

00:01:35.961 --> 00:01:39.865
complete this CAPTCHA screen,
identify all the fire hydrants,

00:01:39.865 --> 00:01:42.568
stop lights, and bridges.
It's a bit much.

00:01:42.568 --> 00:01:44.036
So I say, "You know what?

00:01:44.036 --> 00:01:45.505
Somebody confirmed it
on YouTube."

00:01:45.505 --> 00:01:48.074
And she goes, "Why didn't you
say that in the first place?"

00:01:48.074 --> 00:01:51.210
And then I tell her,
"Because I'm kidding."

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:54.780
It's actually because I know
way too many vengeful,

00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:57.116
spiteful, petty people
who've died

00:01:57.116 --> 00:01:59.985
that would have come back a long
time ago to haunt somebody,

00:01:59.985 --> 00:02:01.487
anybody if they could.

00:02:01.487 --> 00:02:04.924
It takes one to know one, and
I'm that type of person, Jimmy.

00:02:04.924 --> 00:02:06.759
I'm "petty" petty.

00:02:06.759 --> 00:02:08.127
-You are petty?
-Can't help it.

00:02:08.127 --> 00:02:10.630
I'm still mad at you
for something you said to me

00:02:10.630 --> 00:02:13.466
on a random Tuesday morning
in 2009.

00:02:13.466 --> 00:02:14.667
[ Light laughter ]

00:02:14.667 --> 00:02:16.169
I never got over it.

00:02:16.169 --> 00:02:17.903
I'm not gonna say
what it is right now,

00:02:17.903 --> 00:02:20.206
but if I die
and come back as a ghost,

00:02:20.206 --> 00:02:22.441
I'll for sure remind you of it,
maybe --

00:02:22.441 --> 00:02:24.210
[ Laughter ]
-Wait, wait, I'm sorry --

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:25.478
So, you're going to haunt me?

00:02:25.478 --> 00:02:27.847
-Yeah, maybe
for all of eternity.

00:02:27.847 --> 00:02:31.016
So, I'm up now.
I can't get back to sleep.

00:02:31.016 --> 00:02:32.452
That wakes up my wife.

00:02:32.452 --> 00:02:34.787
Instinctively, she immediately
does something that irks me,

00:02:34.787 --> 00:02:39.325
because for her not to do so
would be too much like right.

00:02:39.325 --> 00:02:41.126
She says, "Babe, you're up?"

00:02:41.126 --> 00:02:43.062
I go, "No.

00:02:43.062 --> 00:02:45.364
I'm fast asleep, Michelle.

00:02:45.364 --> 00:02:46.632
I'm sound asleep.

00:02:46.632 --> 00:02:49.969
I'm in the Land of Nod
right now."

00:02:49.969 --> 00:02:52.971
And she goes,
"It's 3:00 a.m. in the morning."

00:02:52.971 --> 00:02:55.141
And that's like nails
on a chalkboard for me,

00:02:55.141 --> 00:02:57.309
because the fact
that you said "a.m."

00:02:57.309 --> 00:03:00.480
is already indicative
of it being in the morning.

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:03.382
We didn't need both.
It's one or the other.

00:03:03.382 --> 00:03:06.185
So consider yourself irk-listed.
-Okay, alright, yeah, okay.

00:03:06.185 --> 00:03:09.722
-I mean, at this point,
she basically has a high score.

00:03:09.722 --> 00:03:11.190
Now I'm wide-awake.

00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:13.726
I'm wide-awake, man.
I'm "woke" woke.

00:03:13.726 --> 00:03:15.862
So I go, hey, I'm going to try
and get some work done.

00:03:15.862 --> 00:03:18.464
And she's all,
"This is a personal problem.

00:03:18.464 --> 00:03:19.732
You know, I could care less."

00:03:19.732 --> 00:03:23.369
And it irks me
that we're cool as a society

00:03:23.369 --> 00:03:25.605
with the saying,
"I could care less."

00:03:25.605 --> 00:03:27.173
But we've unanimously agreed

00:03:27.173 --> 00:03:30.142
that it means we actually
could not care less.

00:03:30.142 --> 00:03:31.710
One could even
split the difference

00:03:31.710 --> 00:03:34.347
and use the word couldn't,
but we just can't be bothered

00:03:34.347 --> 00:03:38.551
with the business of adding
that one apostrophe "nt"

00:03:38.551 --> 00:03:40.019
and making it official.

00:03:40.019 --> 00:03:42.254
So, like, I'm a little angry,
just a little bit,

00:03:42.254 --> 00:03:44.156
you know what I mean?
I'm not "angry" angry.

00:03:44.156 --> 00:03:45.891
But I'm a little irked.

00:03:45.891 --> 00:03:47.226
-Yeah.
-I jump in the shower.

00:03:47.226 --> 00:03:48.895
You ever take
a irk shower, Jimmy?

00:03:48.895 --> 00:03:51.164
-Have I ever --
Have I ever taken irked shower?

00:03:51.164 --> 00:03:53.065
No, I --
-It's abrasive.

00:03:53.065 --> 00:03:54.466
You could hurt yourself.
-Uh-huh.

00:03:54.466 --> 00:03:57.670
So in my attempts to calm down,
I sing a song.

00:03:57.670 --> 00:03:59.438
-Okay.
-And when I sing in the shower,

00:03:59.438 --> 00:04:02.108
I go old-school.
I want some funky ad-libs.

00:04:02.108 --> 00:04:05.345
I come from days when singers
would get fifty-eleven syllables

00:04:05.345 --> 00:04:07.646
out of like a one-syllable word.
-Fifty-eleven?

00:04:07.646 --> 00:04:11.350
-Yeah, yeah, but this new R&amp;B,
man, they only got two ad-libs.

00:04:11.350 --> 00:04:13.485
They go, "Yah. Ey.

00:04:13.485 --> 00:04:15.121
Ey. Yah.

00:04:15.121 --> 00:04:16.756
Yah-yah. Ey-ey."

00:04:16.756 --> 00:04:18.324
It irks me. It irks me, man.

00:04:18.324 --> 00:04:19.759
Back in the day,

00:04:19.759 --> 00:04:23.362
those jokers would made "Yeah"
a 9-, 10-, 11-syllable word,

00:04:23.362 --> 00:04:24.464
talkin' 'bout,

00:04:24.464 --> 00:04:29.801
♪ Yea-ea-ea-ea-a-a-a-a-a-a-a-h ♪

00:04:29.801 --> 00:04:32.938
Now...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:32.938 --> 00:04:34.040
...that's flavor.

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:35.908
Like, we should bring back
words like that,

00:04:35.908 --> 00:04:38.110
words like ♪ Wah-boh ♪

00:04:38.110 --> 00:04:40.213
We need to add more flavor.
-Oh, yeah, I know "wah-boh."

00:04:40.213 --> 00:04:41.647
-Yeah! Come on, more funkiness.
-Yeah. ♪ Wah-boh ♪

00:04:41.647 --> 00:04:44.850
-You ever hear that song
"Get Off Your Ass and Jam"?

00:04:44.850 --> 00:04:46.552
Well, first of all,
it was the profanity

00:04:46.552 --> 00:04:49.388
that drew me in as a kid.
I was maybe 3 years old.

00:04:49.388 --> 00:04:51.657
It was genius.
I'm not going to curse up here,

00:04:51.657 --> 00:04:54.126
but I'll sing it
in pig Latin for you.

00:04:54.126 --> 00:04:55.594
It goes, uh...

00:04:55.594 --> 00:04:56.695
[Bleep]

00:04:56.695 --> 00:04:59.232
"God am-day,
get off your ass and j--"

00:04:59.232 --> 00:05:00.833
Well, there's no pig-Latin word
for ass.

00:05:00.833 --> 00:05:02.301
-Yeah, okay, alright,
that didn't help at all.

00:05:02.301 --> 00:05:03.602
That didn't help.

00:05:03.602 --> 00:05:05.704
-But then they hit you
with that ♪ Wah-boh ♪

00:05:05.704 --> 00:05:07.873
And, oh, man,
that's like the secret weapon.

00:05:07.873 --> 00:05:11.043
That's the sauce, Jimmy.
So it makes it "funky" funky.

00:05:11.043 --> 00:05:13.346
Man, you singing some funk
ad-libs in the shower,

00:05:13.346 --> 00:05:14.780
and you can't stay mad.

00:05:14.780 --> 00:05:17.116
So I get out happy,
and I reach for a towel,

00:05:17.116 --> 00:05:20.119
but then I'm immediately pissed
right back off into irkdom.

00:05:20.119 --> 00:05:22.388
The towel is non-absorbent.

00:05:22.388 --> 00:05:23.756
What am I supposed to do

00:05:23.756 --> 00:05:27.059
with a towel that just
relocates the wetness?

00:05:27.059 --> 00:05:29.128
This towel,
it was giving me nothing.

00:05:29.128 --> 00:05:32.398
So, I go,
"You got one job, towel!

00:05:32.398 --> 00:05:34.300
The hell is your problem?
Stay thirsty, man!

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:35.568
Get your head in the game."

00:05:35.568 --> 00:05:36.902
[ Laughter ]

00:05:36.902 --> 00:05:39.104
"You know, when you were
a little wash cloth,

00:05:39.104 --> 00:05:40.640
I thought you had promise.

00:05:40.640 --> 00:05:43.075
I watched you grow
into a hand towel

00:05:43.075 --> 00:05:45.844
and then a full-on bath towel.

00:05:45.844 --> 00:05:47.413
But right now, right now,

00:05:47.413 --> 00:05:49.848
you acting like
a little beach...towel

00:05:49.848 --> 00:05:51.083
right now.

00:05:51.083 --> 00:05:53.952
Actually, you're giving me
lettuce vibes, man."

00:05:53.952 --> 00:05:56.889
That's what it was, Jimmy.
Like, the towel had a heft

00:05:56.889 --> 00:05:59.558
comparable to that
of a wet leaf of lettuce.

00:05:59.558 --> 00:06:02.895
So I'm basically trying
to dry off with a Caesar salad

00:06:02.895 --> 00:06:04.363
before I decided, you know,

00:06:04.363 --> 00:06:06.065
to just use
a bunch of paper towels.

00:06:06.065 --> 00:06:08.834
Needless to say, the day started
on a bit of a sour note.

00:06:08.834 --> 00:06:11.904
But right now, I'm great, man.
So thanks for asking.

00:06:11.904 --> 00:06:14.407
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:14.407 --> 00:06:17.243
-Wow.

00:06:17.243 --> 00:06:19.679
Tariq Trotter, everybody!
Thank goodness.

00:06:19.679 --> 00:06:20.713
Better now.

